      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Verify Ollama API keys on an authenticated endpoint",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- stop treating the public `/api/tags` catalog as API-key verification\n- validate the key against authenticated `/api/web_search` without performing a search, accepting only the observed authenticated success/query-validation responses\n- trim the key, preserve cancellation, and keep 401/403 mapped to the actionable invalid/revoked error\n- fail closed on unproven statuses and reject insecure or cross-origin credential endpoints before transport\n- retain contributor credit and add a changelog entry thanking @joeVenner\n\n## Maintainer hardening\n\n- `200` and the live authenticated empty-query `400` response prove validation; the originally proposed `422` allowance was removed because it was not observed\n- the public catalog is fetched only after validation and its own 401/403 responses remain credential failures\n- custom transport seams derive validation on the catalog origin, require HTTPS or loopback HTTP, and reject an explicit cross-origin validation URL before attaching credentials\n- cancellation remains cancellation at both network stages instead of becoming a retryable provider error\n\n## Proof\n\nExact head: `16defab547d5551518e7a31a09bc43ab26ee10a9`\n\n- Public Model Identifier Gate: **PASS**; this is model-free behavior plumbing.\n- Real endpoint matrix, with no secret output: missing key returned 401, deliberately invalid key returned 401, and the saved valid key reached the authenticated empty-query validation response (400).\n- Focused `OllamaUsageFetcherRetryMappingTests`: 17 passed.\n- `make check`: passed with zero formatting or lint violations.\n- `make test`: all 50 shards passed.\n- Structured branch review: clean after adding second-stage catalog authorization and endpoint-origin coverage.\n- Developer-ID signed debug package: `CodexGitCommit=16defab5`; deep/strict signature valid; Gatekeeper accepted. App binary SHA-256 `c98b81e440361e4283ca400e8ca0d8e81fff8286e1bd2ec363b95b5843909ad1`; bundled CLI SHA-256 `22c7062b3c9fe0640aee76a61bf2e4ab92a63210608f1cb4feaf220c98114ecc`.\n- Exact bundled CLI with the saved valid key exited 0 and rendered Ollama API-key state. A deliberately invalid key exited 1 with the invalid/revoked remediation.\n- Exact signed app, isolated to Ollama API mode, refreshed successfully and showed the verified-key/no-cloud-quota state as updated just now.\n- Screenshot stayed local; debug preferences were restored byte-identically and the production app remained running.\n- Dependencies unchanged; no dependency-freshness audit required.\n\n## Risk\n\nLow and isolated to Ollama API-key validation. The validation request uses an empty query and performs no search. The accepted status set is deliberately narrow and fails closed if provider behavior changes.\n",
        "branch": "fix/ollama-hourly-window",
